Machine-level English reading of linked-executable.x86-64.disasm.txt
===================================================

Source: ../linked-executable.x86-64.disasm.txt
Historical x86-64 ELF disassembly; instruction addresses in the standalone
object are not absolute linked addresses. This is a first-pass annotated
concordance of printed instruction starts and encodings; individual prose
is NOT a verified state-transformer implementation.

Every INSTRUCTION line is machine-byte evidence followed by a long English
operation name and an operand-specific explanatory sentence. A relocation
is included on the same record. In normal non-branching execution the next
execution index is the byte address of the following instruction, not the
number of the next displayed line. See accompanying machine-state document.

No claim is made that all displayed branches were executed or that code
inside external shared libraries is present here.

INSTRUCTION 0001 | 0x1000 | 48 83 ec 08 | sub    rsp,0x8
  Section or entry point: _init.
  Long operation: Subtract fixed-width integers and update arithmetic condition flags.
  Detailed first-pass effect: Read current rsp and 0x8; subtract source from destination at the destination's encoded integer width and store the low-width result in rsp; set the defined carry, overflow, sign, zero, parity and auxiliary flags (subject to exact width and operands).
  Sequential successor if not otherwise redirected or faulting: 0x1004 (4 bytes).
  Link-time relocation: none.

INSTRUCTION 0002 | 0x1004 | 48 8b 05 b5 3f 00 00 | mov    rax,QWORD PTR [rip+0x3fb5]        # 4fc0 <__gmon_start__@Base>
  Section or entry point: _init.
  Long operation: Copy one operand's exact-width value without performing arithmetic.
  Detailed first-pass effect: Read QWORD PTR [rip+0x3fb5]        # 4fc0 <__gmon_start__@Base> at the width indicated by this encoding and write the resulting bit pattern to rax. If this writes a 32-bit general register, its encompassing 64-bit register has its upper 32 bits cleared. A memory read/write is observable; condition flags do not change.
  Sequential successor if not otherwise redirected or faulting: 0x100b (7 bytes).
  Link-time relocation: none.

INSTRUCTION 0003 | 0x100b | 48 85 c0 | test   rax,rax
  Section or entry point: _init.
  Long operation: Compare bit patterns by computing AND flags without storing a result.
  Detailed first-pass effect: Compute a bitwise AND of rax with rax only for condition flags. Set zero/sign/parity from the masked result; clear carry/overflow, leave auxiliary-carry undefined, and do not write either operand.
  Sequential successor if not otherwise redirected or faulting: 0x100e (3 bytes).
  Link-time relocation: none.

INSTRUCTION 0004 | 0x100e | 74 02 | je     1012 <_init+0x12>
  Section or entry point: _init.
  Long operation: Branch only if zero flag is set.
  Detailed first-pass effect: Evaluate zero flag is set (ZF=1); if true replace the execution index with target 1012 <_init+0x12>; otherwise continue at the sequential next instruction. No general-purpose register or ordinary data memory is written by this branch.
  Sequential successor if not otherwise redirected or faulting: 0x1010 (2 bytes).
  Link-time relocation: none.

INSTRUCTION 0005 | 0x1010 | ff d0 | call   rax
  Section or entry point: _init.
  Long operation: Save the return execution index and transfer to the called routine.
  Detailed first-pass effect: Save byte address 0x1012 as the machine return address by allocating a stack slot, then set the execution index to the call target rax. A pending relocation may replace the printed object target; callee effects and external-library bodies are not supplied by this instruction alone.
  Sequential successor if not otherwise redirected or faulting: 0x1012 (2 bytes).
  Link-time relocation: none.

INSTRUCTION 0006 | 0x1012 | 48 83 c4 08 | add    rsp,0x8
  Section or entry point: _init.
  Long operation: Add fixed-width integers and update arithmetic condition flags.
  Detailed first-pass effect: Read current rsp and 0x8; add source to destination at the destination's encoded integer width and store the low-width result in rsp; set the defined carry, overflow, sign, zero, parity and auxiliary flags (subject to exact width and operands).
  Sequential successor if not otherwise redirected or faulting: 0x1016 (4 bytes).
  Link-time relocation: none.

INSTRUCTION 0007 | 0x1016 | c3 | ret
  Section or entry point: _init.
  Long operation: Transfer execution back to the address stored on the call stack.
  Detailed first-pass effect: Read an eight-byte return address from the stack, release the slot by advancing RSP, and replace the execution index with that address (subject to platform control-flow checks and faults). This is not sequential instruction advancement.
  Sequential successor if not otherwise redirected or faulting: 0x1017 (1 byte).
  Link-time relocation: none.

